# removing_digits:
# CSES 1637, Removing Digits (https://cses.fi/problemset/task/1637), in our own
# words: starting from a positive integer number, each step subtracts one of the
# nonzero decimal digits of the current number; the fewest steps that reach
# zero. The input is a binary natural number, the answer a binary natural. Part of the
# CSES port's second batch.
#
# THE PROGRAM, written by the definition: the list of the lengths of all step
# sequences from number down to zero is built (the list holding 0 when number is zero,
# otherwise, for each nonzero decimal digit of number, the lengths of the sequences
# from number - digit, each plus one), and its least member taken. The decimal digits are
# found by repeated division by ten, written bit by bit from the low end of the
# binary numeral (ten_divmod). Its reading is exponential in number even under
# tabling, since every step sequence is counted; the replacement the family asks
# for is the one-dimensional recurrence fewest(number) = 1 + min over the nonzero
# digits of number of fewest(number - digit), on fixed-width integers.
#
# DEFINITION 14: the program P, the point's term, is built of λ and application
# only: its text holds no top, no choice, no parallel and no literal (the ten is
# written with binary_zero, binary_even and binary_odd). It β-reduces to V, the
# canonical binary numeral of the answer: every recursion ends, since ten_divmod
# and digits consume a binary numeral (the quotient by ten of a positive number is
# smaller, and the recursion of digits stops at zero), step_lengths consumes number, which
# falls by a nonzero digit at each call, and every other recursion consumes a
# finite list. So the β reduction reaches V; the branches that a Scott boolean
# discards are never read. binary_subtract, which writes no top
# (../common/binary_modular), is never asked for less than zero: it subtracts
# ten from a remainder only when the remainder is not below ten, and a digit
# from the number that has it. So ⊢_β P = V, and P ≃_O V by the soundness of
# the derivable equations for the contextual preorder of Definition 14 (Lean
# `ContextualPreorder.contextualEquivalenceOfDerivableLatticeEta`): V is an
# answer, P ⊑_O V. No other closed βη normal form W has P ⊑_O W: then V ⊑_O W,
# while Böhm's theorem gives a pure context that takes V to λx y. x and W to
# λx y. y, and applying both to λa. a and Ω makes the first solvable and the
# second not.
λ export
. (λtuple. tuple λmixin. mixin mixin)
λ omega
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "fixpoint")
λ fixpoint
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "boolean")
λ _ false _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "prelude") "list")
λ nil cons append map _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "natural")
λ binary_zero binary_even binary_odd _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "arithmetic")
λ merge_binary_increment _ _ _
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "corpora") "library") "binary") "order")
λ binary_less_than _ binary_minimum
. omega (omega (omega (omega (omega gezi "problems") "cses") "common") "binary_modular")
λ binary_double binary_subtract _ _
. (λtuple. tuple (binary_even λ. binary_odd λ. binary_even λ. binary_odd binary_zero))
λ ten
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself function items. items nil λhead tail. append (function head) λ. self function tail
  )
λ concat_map
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ quotient remainder continue
    . binary_less_than remainder ten (continue (binary_double quotient) remainder) (continue (binary_odd quotient) (binary_subtract remainder ten false))
  )
λ settle
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self natural
    . natural (λcontinue. continue binary_zero binary_zero)
      (λhalf continue. self half λquotient remainder. settle quotient (binary_double remainder) continue)
      λhalf continue. self half λquotient remainder. settle quotient (binary_odd remainder) continue
  )
λ ten_divmod
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self number
    . number nil (λ_. ten_divmod number λquotient digit. cons digit λ. self quotient) λ_. ten_divmod number λquotient digit. cons digit λ. self quotient
  )
λ digits
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple
    λ. fixpoint
    λ self number
    . ( λ step
        . number (cons binary_zero nil) (λ_. step) λ_. step
      )
      ( concat_map
        ( λ digit
          . digit nil
            (λ_. map merge_binary_increment λ. self λ. binary_subtract number digit false)
            λ_. map merge_binary_increment λ. self λ. binary_subtract number digit false
        ) λ. digits number
      )
  )
λ step_lengths
. ( λ tuple
    . tuple λ. fixpoint λself least candidates. candidates least λcandidate rest. self (binary_minimum least candidate) rest
  )
λ fold_minimum
. (λtuple. tuple λnumber. step_lengths number binary_zero λhead tail. fold_minimum head tail)
λ removing_digits
. export removing_digits
